{"nodes": [{"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_state", "label": "state (app-level state bag)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Plain JS with no reactive framework: every change re-renders by hand, because for a multi-frontend comparison the load-bearing part is the WebSocket + audio plumbing, not the UI."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_decodeincoming", "label": "decodeIncoming (plain copy)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_shared_frame_codec", "label": "shared/frameCodec.ts (hand-duplicated codec)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The build-free frontends cannot import the TypeScript codec, so decodeIncoming is copied into each single-file app with an explicit keep-in-sync comment \u2014 the duplication is the price of having no build step."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_connectandsend", "label": "connectAndSend", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_scheduleresume", "label": "scheduleResume", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exponential backoff capped at 4 s over at most MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS tries, and only when a session token exists \u2014 a socket that closes without a token is a logout, not a dropout."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_cancelreconnect", "label": "cancelReconnect", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_resettogate", "label": "resetToGate", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hard reload rather than incremental teardown: the simplest correct cleanup for a demo."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_handleservertext", "label": "handleServerText", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_handleserverbinary", "label": "handleServerBinary", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_startmicmeterloop", "label": "startMicMeterLoop", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Peak deviation from 128 (the zero point of 8-bit PCM) is used as the level, sampled on requestAnimationFrame so the meter costs nothing when the tab is hidden."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_wirepttbutton", "label": "wirePttButton", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pointer events cover mouse, touch and pen uniformly, and the pointer is captured on press so an up-event outside the button still ends the transmission instead of leaving the mic open."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_beginpress", "label": "beginPress", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Target selection is sent before the first audio chunk, so the server always knows where a stream is going before any of it arrives."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_endpress", "label": "endPress", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_toggleroomtalk", "label": "toggleRoomTalk", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Room talk is open-mic, not push-to-talk: it stays on until toggled off or the room is left."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_startmicrecording", "label": "startMicRecording", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_stopmicrecording", "label": "stopMicRecording", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_startincoming", "label": "startIncoming", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_feedincoming", "label": "feedIncoming", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The opus view is copied before queueing because it is a subarray onto a larger buffer that may be reclaimed, and SourceBuffer wants its own buffer."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_drainqueue", "label": "drainQueue", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Appends one chunk at a time and swallows appendBuffer throws (out-of-quota etc.); the next updateend retries, so a transient failure drops a chunk instead of killing the stream."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_endincoming", "label": "endIncoming", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Teardown is delayed ~1.5 s so the already-appended buffer flushes audibly before the audio element and its object URL are revoked."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_rendertalking", "label": "renderTalking", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_enterapp", "label": "enterApp", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_mic_gesture_unlock", "label": "One-time mic gesture unlocking capture and playback", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single 'Enable mic' click does double duty: it grants the getUserMedia permission and it resumes the AudioContext, because modern browsers gate inbound playback behind a user gesture too \u2014 without it received audio would be silent even though capture worked."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_fresh_mediarecorder_per_press", "label": "Fresh MediaRecorder per press", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first chunk of every MediaRecorder run carries the WebM init segment and later chunks are media segments; receivers depend on that, so each voice-incoming-start opens a fresh MediaSource whose first append is the init."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_hidden_attribute_specificity_fix", "label": "[hidden] display:none !important specificity fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The UA stylesheet maps the hidden attribute to display:none, but a class rule like .app { display: grid } outranks it and would leave the gate and the app pane visible at once; pinning [hidden] with !important makes the attribute do what its name says."}, {"id": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_phase_machine", "label": "Phase machine: gate-mic to gate-login to app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "examples/voice/static/plain/index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_connectandsend", "target": "examples_voice_static_plain_index_handleservertext", "relation": "calls", "confidence"